ROOM CODE AND TEAM CODE SYSTEM:

There must be TWO COMPLETELY DISTINCT CODES.

ROOM CODE:
Identifies a particular competition room.

TEAM CODE:
Identifies the campus or team represented by a participant.

Example:

Competition Room:
3977-CTF-82A

Campus A:
CAMPUS-001

Campus B:
CAMPUS-002

Campus C:
CAMPUS-003

All players participating in the same competition enter the same Room Code.

Players enter their own campus Team Code.

One competition room can contain many campus teams.

JOIN FLOW:

1. Player logs in.
2. Player selects Join Competition.
3. Player enters Room Code.
4. Player enters Team Code.
5. Server validates both codes.
6. Server verifies eligibility and capacity.
7. Player joins the correct team lobby.

Never trust frontend-only code validation.

CAPACITY:

Make room capacity and team capacity configurable.

Example initial event:
- 150 total participants.
- 30 players per campus team.
- 5 campus teams.

Do not hardcode these limits.

CODE MANAGEMENT:

Authorized admins can:
- Create codes.
- View codes according to permission.
- Regenerate codes.
- Revoke codes.
- Disable codes.
- Set expiration.
- Set usage limits.
- Configure code access policies.

Changing a code must invalidate the previous code immediately.

Support configurable team enrollment policies:
- Shared campus team codes.
- Individual player invitations.
- Organizer approval.
- Campus verification.

The owner can select which enrollment policy is used for each competition.

TEAM MANAGEMENT:

- Team name.
