21. PERMISSION SYSTEM
==================================================

Use strict server-side Role-Based Access Control.

OWNER:
Full platform access.

EVENT ADMIN:
Access only to assigned events and explicitly granted functions.

MODERATOR:
Limited moderation permissions for assigned events.

TEAM CAPTAIN:
Manage permitted team activities and communication.

PLAYER:
Participate in allowed activities.

Permissions must be individually configurable.

Do not trust role names or permission flags submitted by the browser.

Every sensitive API endpoint must validate the authenticated user's authorization.

Admins must not grant themselves additional permissions.

Only the owner can appoint or revoke administrators.

Record all privileged actions in audit logs.

